silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_concrete_anchor_3 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "NegativeWitnessAnchorEmptyHomSetExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_15_witness_traceability_sections_04_negative_witnesses_concrete_anchor_3 silm:hasExample "In 'NegativeWitnessAnchorEmptyHomSet', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, EmptyHomSet is the terminus of the gate_refuse arrow in the negative-witness chain. For the catus-collision probe, the empty hom-set is Hom_O_01(catus, Mittens) = empty: there is no admitted arrow from a bare catus row to the concrete cat Mittens. The negative witness from gippidy00 lines 97-105 (collision-list) supports this empty hom-set by enumerating the candidates that fail (bare catus, TSN 183798 alone, any catus row) and exhibiting why each cannot be Mittens.." .
